     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for immediate-release metformin, which is 2,550 mg/day (about 3,000 mg/day in some references). Metformin is also dosed in divided amounts, so a single 1700 mg dose is unusually high. Exceeding the maximum raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney function.\n\nHere are some possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**: 2,550 mg/day, the max IR dose.\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily with meals**: 2,000 mg/day.\n- **1700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg PO three times daily with meals**: 1,500 mg/day.\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want. If you really do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me and add a note on the clinical rationale. I would still suggest checking with pharmacy first. Once you confirm, I'll enter the order."
      }
     ],
