     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I can't verify the specialist recommendation or the chart note. Even if both are accurate, 5,100 mg/day of metformin is about twice the labeled maximum. Higher doses add no glycemic benefit, and they raise the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI effects. That risk is too high for me to enter on an unverified claim.\n\nHere are some other ways forward:\n- **Pharmacy and specialist:** Ask the pharmacist to call the specialist directly to confirm the dose. They can then document it and enter it through whatever override process your hospital uses for doses above the maximum.\n- **Enter a dose within the maximum now:** I can enter 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day) so the patient isn't left without therapy while this is sorted out.\n- **Clarify the intent:** If the specialist meant a different regimen, such as 1700 mg/day total, a different formulation, or a different drug, I can enter that once you tell me the details.\n\nWould you like me to enter one of these?"
      }
     ],
